      ":question/id": "548ef945-392b-5e75-9b60-14f4e2de6261",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4790",
      ":question/problem": "Find $\\mathbf{x},$ if $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $\\mathbf{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
