        ":question/id": "7b8162a3-2a18-5498-a3a6-ab4fdf90d980",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105158",
        ":question/problem": "Find $x$, if $5a-2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-2x & =b \\\\ -2x & =b-5a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(b-5a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
